# C# Coding Standards

## 🎯 **General Principles**

### **Clean Architecture Compliance:**
- **Domain Layer**: Pure business logic, no external dependencies
- **Application Layer**: Orchestrates domain logic, defines interfaces
- **Infrastructure Layer**: Implements external concerns (database, email, etc.)
- **Presentation Layer**: Handles HTTP requests, minimal business logic

### **Dependency Injection:**
- Use constructor injection for all dependencies
- Register services in appropriate `*DependencyInjection.cs` files
- Prefer interfaces over concrete implementations

## 📝 **Code Style**

### **Naming Conventions:**
```csharp
// Classes and Interfaces
public class AccountService : IAccountService
public interface IRepository<T> where T : class

// Methods and Properties
public async Task<AccountDTO> CreateAccountAsync(CreateAccountDTO dto)
public string FirstName { get; set; }

// Constants and Enums
public enum RoleEnum
{
    SuperAdmin = 1,
    Admin
}

// Private fields
private readonly IRepository<Account> _accountRepository;
```

### **Async/Await Patterns:**
```csharp
// Always use async/await for I/O operations
public async Task<AccountDTO> GetAccountAsync(int id)
{
    var account = await _accountRepository.GetByIdAsync(id);
    return _mapper.Map<AccountDTO>(account);
}

// Use ConfigureAwait(false) in library code
await SomeOperationAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);
```

## 🏗️ **Entity Framework Patterns**

### **DbContext Usage:**
- Use [ApplicationDbContext.cs](mdc:ApiTemplate.Infrastructure/ApplicationDbContext.cs) as the main context
- Configure UTC datetime conversion globally
- Use Identity integration for user management

### **Repository Pattern:**
```csharp
// Generic repository interface
public interface IRepository<T> where T : class
{
    Task<T?> GetByIdAsync(int id);
    Task<IEnumerable<T>> GetAllAsync();
    Task<T> AddAsync(T entity);
    Task UpdateAsync(T entity);
    Task DeleteAsync(int id);
}
```

### **Entity Configuration:**
```csharp
// Use Data Annotations for simple configurations
[MaxLength(250)]
public string FirstName { get; set; }

// Use Fluent API for complex relationships
builder.Entity<AccountTokenEntity>()
    .HasOne(x => x.User)
    .WithMany(x => x.Tokens)
    .HasForeignKey(x => x.UserId);
```

## 🔐 **Security Patterns**

### **Authentication & Authorization:**
```csharp
// Use ASP.NET Core Identity
public class Account : IdentityUser<int>

// Custom authorization attributes
[AuthorizeRoles(RoleEnum.Admin)]
public async Task<IActionResult> AdminOnlyAction()

// JWT configuration in appsettings.json
"Jwt": {
    "LifetimeMinutes": 30,
    "Key": "ihopethiskeyislongenough",
    "Issuer": "web-api-template"
}
```

### **Input Validation:**
```csharp
// Use Data Annotations
public class CreateAccountDTO
{
    [Required]
    [EmailAddress]
    public string Email { get; set; }
    
    [Required]
    [MinLength(6)]
    public string Password { get; set; }
}
```

## 📊 **Logging & Monitoring**

### **Structured Logging:**
```csharp
// Use Serilog with structured logging
_logger.LogInformation("User {UserId} created account {Email}", userId, email);

// Use correlation IDs
_logger.LogInformation("Processing request {RequestId}", correlationId);
```

### **Exception Handling:**
```csharp
// Custom domain exceptions
public class DomainException : Exception
{
    public DomainException(string message) : base(message) { }
}

// Global exception handling in Program.cs
webApplication.HandleExceptions();
```

## 🧪 **Testing Patterns**

### **Unit Test Structure:**
```csharp
// Use AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert)
[Test]
public async Task CreateAccount_ValidInput_ReturnsAccountDTO()
{
    // Arrange
    var dto = new CreateAccountDTO { Email = "test@example.com" };
    
    // Act
    var result = await _accountService.CreateAccountAsync(dto);
    
    // Assert
    Assert.That(result.Email, Is.EqualTo(dto.Email));
}
```

### **Integration Test Base:**
- Use [BaseIntegrationTest.cs](mdc:ApiTemplate.Presentation.Web.Tests.Integration/BaseIntegrationTest.cs)
- Test with real database and HTTP client
- Use test-specific configuration

## 🔧 **Configuration Management**

### **appsettings.json Structure:**
```json
{
  "ConnectionStrings": {
    "MSSQL": "Server=localhost,1433;Database=webapi;..."
  },
  "Jwt": {
    "LifetimeMinutes": 30,
    "Key": "ihopethiskeyislongenough"
  },
  "SMTPConfiguration": {
    "Host": "smtp.gmail.com",
    "Port": 587
  }
}
```

### **Environment-Specific Configuration:**
- Use `appsettings.Development.json` for local development
- Use ConfigMaps in Kubernetes for containerized environments
- Never commit sensitive data (use secrets)